   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've added $5.60 in credit to your account. You can use it on a future order. Late deliveries are compensated with account credit only, not a refund to your card.\n\nI'm sorry dinner arrived so late. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Five dollars and sixty cents in credit? I was promised dinner at 7 and it showed up at 7:45, cold and after I'd already given up on it. Credit I might use someday isn't really compensation for that. And I'm not sure why the app says it was delivered at 7 when nothing was there."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand why that's frustrating. Dinner arrived 47 minutes late, and the app said it was delivered when it wasn't.\n\nThe app showed 7:00 because the courier's app marked the order delivered at 6:58 PM, while they were still 2.1 miles away. That was an error. The courier's log shows the real handoff at 7:47 PM, so I used that time for your compensation.\n\nThe $5.60 is what our policy gives for this much lateness. It's 20% of your $28.00 subtotal, and late deliveries get account credit only. I can't refund the card or add more credit. I don't have a policy basis for goodwill extras, even though the delay was real.\n\nIf you want, I can pass this to a person on our team. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Fine, I'd like that. Credit that only works on a future order doesn't cover the wait I actually had, so I want someone to look at a refund or a better offer. Please don't make me repeat all of this to them, either. Leo Brandt, order 7201, phone 415-555-0232."
  },
